%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
title: b1 Welcoming, introducing and following up
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Nine objectives, three use cases, six functions. UC01: welcoming a newcomer. UC02: introducing two residents, the main use case. UC03: following up an agreed meeting, or a resident who has been staying in their room. Six Premises verify that the Functions work; nine Claims, four of them adverse, test whether they help.

= Objectives =

== Objective - Residents meet again [OBJ-01] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-01
|Name|Residents meet again
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Goal on SA-03; PS-03. HFC-15, HFC-16.
|Statement|Introductions lead to second meetings and, over weeks, to friendships.
|Type|Human-factors
|Derived from|Goal on SA-03; HFC-15 Similarity and shared background; HFC-16 Fear of rejection and the liking gap
|Priority|Must.

== Objective - Newcomers find company [OBJ-02] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-02
|Name|Newcomers find company
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Goal on SA-01; PS-01. HFC-02.
|Statement|In their first weeks, newcomers meet a few residents, keep some of their names, and spend less of the day alone in their room.
|Type|Human-factors
|Derived from|Goal on SA-01; HFC-02 Moving into a care home
|Priority|Must.

== Objective - Time together [OBJ-03] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-03
|Name|Time together
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Goal on SA-04; PS-04. HFC-01. Forbes et al. (2015).
|Statement|Residents who have met spend time together doing something both enjoy. The System may suggest one activity from both residents' preferences; a walk is only one option.
|Type|Operational
|Derived from|Goal on SA-04; HV-05, HV-06; HFC-01
|Priority|Should.

== Objective - No deception [OBJ-04] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-04
|Name|No deception
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|PS-01; VT-03; HFC-08.
|Statement|The System never lies, denies or plays along, and corrects its own errors at once. Painful truths come from a trusted person.
|Type|Value-derived
|Derived from|HV-08 Truthfulness
|Priority|Must.

== Objective - No secret revealed [OBJ-05] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-05
|Name|No secret revealed
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|VT-01, VT-05.
|Statement|Nothing about a resident reaches another person without that resident's consent. Nothing leaves the care home.
|Type|Value-derived
|Derived from|HV-03 Privacy
|Priority|Must.

== Objective - Free to say no [OBJ-06] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-06
|Name|Free to say no
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|VT-02; PS-04; HFC-17. Ryan & Deci (2000).
|Statement|Each resident decides, privately, whether to meet someone. A "no" is final and reaches nobody.
|Type|Value-derived
|Derived from|HV-01 Autonomy; bounded by VT-02
|Priority|Must.

== Objective - Adult voice [OBJ-07] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-07
|Name|Adult voice
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|HFC-06. Williams et al. (2009); Kitwood (1997).
|Statement|No elderspeak, no quizzing, no correcting, no praise for the obvious.
|Type|Value-derived
|Derived from|HV-02 Dignity
|Priority|Should.

== Objective - Less lonely [OBJ-08] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-08
|Name|Less lonely
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|HFC-07; PS-01, PS-02. Victor (2012); Holwerda et al. (2014).
|Statement|Over months, residents feel less lonely.
|Type|Human-factors
|Derived from|HV-06 Social connectedness; HFC-07
|Priority|Should. Exploratory within this project's time frame.

== Objective - Withdrawal noticed [OBJ-09] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-09
|Name|Withdrawal noticed
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Goal on SA-02; PS-02; VT-06; HFC-07.
|Statement|Where a resident agreed, staff hear of a pattern of staying in before mood and mobility decline, without the resident being watched.
|Type|Value-derived
|Derived from|Goal on SA-02; HV-05 Well-being; bounded by VT-06
|Priority|Should.

