UC02: realizes → DS-01; serves → OBJ-01, OBJ-03, OBJ-05 to OBJ-08; uses → TDP-01, IDP-01, IDP-02; asserts → UC02-F1-PR1, UC02-F2-PR2, UC02-F3-PR3, UC02-F6-PR6, UC02-F3-CL1, UC02-F1-CL3, UC02-F2-CL4, UC02-F3-CL9.

UC03: realizes → DS-01; serves → OBJ-01, OBJ-03, OBJ-06, OBJ-09; uses → TDP-01, IDP-02; asserts → UC03-F5-PR5, UC03-F5-CL6, UC03-F5-CL7.

= Open items =

|=ID|=Item|=Blocks|=Owner
|O-1|Resolved. HFC-01 records that the evidence for walking benefits in dementia is weak, so the design presents a walk as one optional activity among several and never as the default.|Nothing|Closed
|O-2|Thresholds: suggestions per week; introductions per newcomer per week; note latency; the presence pattern (days, hours above usual); the trusted person's arrival; System error rate; how long before a declined pair is suggested again. Set from an EM-01 pilot and with care workers.|PR1 to PR5; CL8; VT-02; VT-06|Group
|O-3|Pepper's recognition of older voices, in their own language and dialect. Test in EM-01; the tablet is the fallback.|TECH-01; F1, F4|Group
|O-4|Relationship map and prepared lines: form, owner, review after events; how staff learn of conflicts between residents.|F1 to F4; VT-01|ST-05 with group
|O-5|Consent and data: GDPR art. 6 and 9; the representative's role; process consent; who releases profile items when the resident cannot; check of the local medical-research law.|All pre-conditions; EM-02, EM-03|ST-07
|O-6|Walking policy with ST-07 and ST-06: who may walk in the garden with another resident, and who opens the door.|F3 walk suggestions; UC02|ST-07, ST-06
|O-7|Presence notes: who may opt in, and how assent is recorded; the default pattern for a note; who sees notes; review at each care-plan review.|TECH-03; F5; VT-06|ST-07 with ST-05 and group
|O-8|Pepper in the lounge: a quiet corner for private questions, out of other residents' way. Check on site.|TECH-01; RP-01; F1|Group
|O-9|Comparison home: recruitment, and matching on size, layout and resident mix.|EM-03|Group

= References =

Cited on this page: Bohns (2016); Boothby et al. (2018); Forbes et al. (2015); Holwerda et al. (2014); Kitwood (1997); McPherson et al. (2001); Mental Health Foundation (2016); Niemeijer et al. (2015); Ryan & Deci (2000); Sury et al. (2013); Victor (2012); Williams et al. (2009). Full entries on pages a1.1, b1.1, b3.1 and b4.1.
